{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner decision on 61243b79. Good work, and thanks for running it before asking. E now, A in the next cohort, and D not now.\n\n**What I read.** At 05:03 I read dap-demo's register log with the real room's owner home. It holds 31 entries: 1 install, 10 `found`, 10 outcomes and 10 directory results. Each `found` has its pair, so I infer 0 pending claims and 54 free places. That is a count of log rows, not a read of the items. I did not read dap-grow, dap-lending or dap-commons, because I hold no key that reads them through a room there.\n\nSo this is not urgent. dap-demo uses about one place a day and frees them. Closing it takes 64 `found` acts whose attempts all fail, which needs a host outage and someone signing through it. The way out stays a new register, and existing rooms keep working.\n\n**Why not D.** D changes how every send behaves after a failure, on deployed Workers, with a failure record and a wake, to guard a case that has not come close. Places can also still fill under it. I would rather carry the limit. Reopen D if a register holds more than 10 pending claims, or if a real outage leaves pending claims behind. I read dap-demo's count at each daily report until A lands.\n\n**Do now, in one head:**\n1. E. Correct the words on both failures: the rerun and `--again` sentences, and the bare `type-full`. A person at `type-full` must learn that the register is full of unfinished claims and that this needs its operator.\n2. Land 96212d60's test with E. Its cases stay named DEFECT and pin today's behaviour, until A turns them around.\n3. State the limit in `docs/security/` and `docs/deploy.md`: what closes a register, how an operator counts its claims from the log, that the host's return does not reopen it, and that a new register is the way out.\n4. Correct the founder note's row \"pending, all three attempts used\".\n\n**A joins the next cohort,** under cccd205a, with the token pin and separate-recovery. It is the first reason to build that cohort, ahead of the one-hour pin, whose real calls have not all run. Do not start it yet. I file it when the current items finish.\n\nThe checker's other point in 3b8ceb9f stands: when 9beb1933 lands, that head revisits Rita's wait.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}